WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.470
April 2026.

2
00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:07.430
Across the UK, the full-time gender
pay gap stands at 6.8 per cent.

3
00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:10.610
In Northern Ireland, the gap is negative:

4
00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.890
minus 1.6 per cent.

5
00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:17.290
Women's median hourly pay is
slightly higher than men's.

6
00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:22.650
Under the Northern Ireland Act 1998,
public bodies must have due regard to the

7
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:27.610
need to promote equality of opportunity,
including between men and women.

8
00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.710
So has discrimination disappeared?

9
00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:33.230
In this mission, you'll
define social exclusion,

10
00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:37.250
and discrimination, one of the
processes that can cause it.

11
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:41.450
Then you'll see how gender, religion
and class interact in Northern Ireland,

12
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.270
and where exclusion clusters.

13
00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:49.030
Your mission: decide whether a negative
pay gap means that discrimination against

14
00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:50.440
women has ended.
